      "content": "Focusing on stereotypes based on appearance is a dangerous and biased approach for police training. Instead of relying on race or specific demographics, training should focus strictly on observable, non-discriminatory behaviors. You should train officers to recognize the *actions*—like furtive movements or aggressive posturing—regardless of what the individual is wearing or who they are. Basing threat assessment on appearance alone is inherently flawed and leads to profiling.",
